"""Return to brand, rebuilt around the returnable pool (#75).

Mostly additive. The one destructive part is deliberate: ``credit_note_received``
and ``credit_note_date`` leave the document and become the ``ReturnCreditNote``
companion, because a posted document is immutable at the kernel and a credit note
arrives days or weeks *after* the return posts — the two columns could never have
been written on a real return. Any value an install does hold is carried across
before the columns go, so nothing recorded is lost.
"""

